# Python: the interpreter is KEPT and gets VERSION-BUMPED. Third-party modules
# stay out (every BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON_* below is unset — verified 0 enabled).
#
# Decision 2026-08-19, reversing the removal staged earlier the same day.
#
# The removal case was real: no product component uses python (no reference in
# any init script, CGI or daemon in either tree), the S99python boot hook that
# executed /root/main.py as root went on 2026-08-10, and five of the six bench
# scripts turned out to be network clients that run on the bench PC, not on the
# device — only encoder-sim.py genuinely needs the unit's CAN bus, and its
# candump-log replacement is host-verified. That finding stands and is why the
# canplayer path was built.
#
# It was reversed anyway: keeping a working interpreter on the device is worth
# more than the ~18 MB, and the CVE argument for removal is weaker than it
# looked — see the re-triage of CVE-2020-29396 in scripts/compliance/cve-triage.csv,
# which was never a CPython defect at all.
#
# The five accepted-risk rows are addressed by moving off 3.11.6 instead:
#   CVE-2024-6232   tarfile ReDoS            fixed 3.11.10
#   CVE-2024-7592   http.cookies quadratic   fixed 3.11.10
#   CVE-2026-4519   webbrowser.open dashes   post-3.11.15, expected 3.11.16
#   CVE-2026-15308  html.parser DoS          post-3.11.15, expected 3.11.16
#   CVE-2020-29396  NOT CPython — Odoo sandbox escape, python listed only as the
#                   running-with platform. Re-triaged not-affected; no version
#                   bump would ever have cleared it.
#
# The version pin itself lives in the tracked package replacement
# sysdrv/tools/board/buildroot/python3/ (same mechanism as libopenssl 3.5.7 and
# open62541 1.3.15, copied in by sysdrv/Makefile) — NOT here, and NOT in
# sysdrv/source/buildroot/**, which .gitignore treats as throwaway.
#
# Target is the 3.11 branch (3.11.16, 12 Aug 2026; security-only until Oct 2027).
# 3.12+ is not a version bump but a port: 11 of buildroot 2023.02.6's 31 python3
# patches target files CPython has since deleted or moved — setup.py (7 patches,
# gone in 3.12), Lib/distutils (2, gone in 3.12), Lib/crypt.py (1, gone in 3.13),
# Tools/scripts (1, moved in 3.12) — and patch 0003, the infrastructure the
# module-disable options all rest on, is one of the setup.py ones. The external
# Rockchip toolchain is gcc 8.3.0 and is not ours to move.
#
# PYTHON3_SSL: bench tooling imports ssl. PYTHON3_ZLIB: previously enabled only
# as a side effect of python-pillow; kept explicitly because libzlib is in the
# image regardless (so it adds no component) and a stdlib without it fails in
# ways that look like a bench-script bug.
#
# Two stray scripts, neither of which belongs on a shipped target:
#   /usr/bin/smtpd.py.11  FIXED in the package replacement. CPython's stdlib demo
#                         SMTP *server*, 31 KB and executable, had shipped on PATH
#                         in every image: stock python3.mk removes 'smtpd.py.3',
#                         but CPython installs it as smtpd.py.<minor>, so the rm
#                         had always been a no-op. Now globbed. Takes effect on the
#                         next python3 rebuild.
#   /usr/bin/event_rpcgen.py  STILL PRESENT, and not ours to fix here — it comes
#                         from libevent, not python3. A BUILD tool carrying
#                         `#!/usr/bin/env python`, so already broken today since
#                         there is no python2.
# /sbin/routel (`#!/usr/bin/env python3`) keeps working, since the interpreter stays.
BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON3=y
BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_SSL=y
BR2_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_ZLIB=y
